,"attributes":{"level":3,"id":"name-matching-rule"},"children":["Name Matching Rule"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["In Kilo Code, the ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["name"]}," field ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["must match"]}," the parent directory name:"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Fence","attributes":{},"children":["✅ Correct:\nskills/\n└── frontend-design/\n    └── SKILL.md  # name: frontend-design\n\n❌ Incorrect:\nskills/\n└── frontend-design/\n    └── SKILL.md  # name: my-frontend-skill  (doesn't match!)\n"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Heading","attributes":{"level":2,"id":"optional-bundled-resources"},"children":["Optional Bundled Resources"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["While ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["SKILL.md"]}," is the only required file, you can optionally include additional directories to support your skill:"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Fence","attributes":{},"children":["my-skill/\n├── SKILL.md           # Required: instructions + metadata\n├── scripts/           # Optional: executable code\n├── references/        # Optional: documentation\n└── assets/            # Optional: templates, resources\n"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["These additional files can be referenced from your skill's instructions, allowing the agent to read documentation, execute scripts, or use templates as needed."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Heading","attributes":{"level":2,"id":"shell-commands-in-skills"},"children":["Shell commands in skills"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["A ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["SKILL.md"]}," body can embed shell commands with the ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["!`command`"]}," syntax. When the agent loads the skill, each command runs and its standard output replaces the placeholder before the skill content reaches the model, grounding the skill in live data:"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Fence","attributes":{"data-language":"markdown"},"children":["---\nname: repo-status\ndescription: Summarize the current state of the repository\n---\n\nThe working tree currently contains:\n\n!`git status --short`\n"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Because the agent decides when to load a skill, embedded commands never run silently:"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"ul","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Trusted skills only"]}," — commands execute only in skills from trusted locations: global skills (such as ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["~/.kilo/skills/"]},", ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["~/.agents/skills/"]},", and ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["~/.claude/skills/"]},"), skills built into Kilo Code, and absolute skill paths declared in global config. Project skills (",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":[".kilo/skills/"]}," in a repository) and skills fetched from remote URLs never execute commands; their placeholders are replaced with a marker noting the skill is untrusted."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Approval required"]}," — when the agent loads a trusted skill containing commands, every command in the file is listed in a single permission prompt before anything runs. Approving runs all of them; rejecting aborts the skill load. This prompt appears even when bash commands are otherwise auto-approved, and a deny rule on any command still blocks it."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Kill switch"]}," — set the ",{"$$md